title: EMR Connect › Sync › When an agent is paused or asks first
route: /emr
intro: Four buttons on this page start work that an agent does: Sync now and Connect a system (Reader), Fix and Reconnect (Navigator). Settings decides how each one starts. A paused agent waits, 'Ask before acting' asks first, any other level goes ahead.
dir: TD
also: The choice is read at the moment of the click. Disconnect, the write-back switch and Map are a person's own decisions and are never held back. After the step, 'Act on its own' only logs it in Recent activity.
---
start s1 "Click 'Sync now', 'Connect a system', 'Fix' or 'Reconnect'\nHeader, a row, or the Manage drawer"
decision q1 "Which agent does the step?"
process a1 "Reader\nSync now (header or a row) and Connect a system"
process a2 "Navigator\nFix, and Reconnect on a row or in the Manage drawer"

decision q2 "Is that agent paused in Settings?"
toast t1 "'{Agent} is paused'\n'Resume it in Settings to sync.'\nOr: to connect a system, fix it, reconnect it\nAmber"
endx x1 "Nothing starts\nThe page stays as it was"

decision q3 "What is the agent's Freedom level?"
overlay o1 "Asks first\n'Sync every connected system?', 'Sync {system}?', 'Fix {system}?' or 'Reconnect {system}?'\n'{Agent} is set to Ask before acting'"
process o2 "The pop-up links to Settings\n'Change this for {Agent} in Settings'"
click c1 "Click 'Not now', the X, or press Escape"
endx x2 "Pop-up closes\nNothing starts"
click c2 "Click the step's button\n'Sync now', 'Start the fix' or 'Start'"
process p1 "The step goes ahead at once\nConnect never asks: its own three-step pop-up is the confirmation"

group gAfter "After the step finishes"
  agent r1 "The agent logs one line in Recent activity\nEvery level does this"
  decision q4 "Is the agent set to 'Act on its own'?"
  process n1 "No toast\nThe tiles and the log show what happened"
  toast t2 "A toast says what happened\n'Sync finished', '{name} is connected' or 'Sign-in renewed'"
endgroup

goto g1 "Continues in: EMR Connect › Sync › Sync now"
goto g2 "Continues in: EMR Connect › Problems › Fix a system that needs a quick look"
goto g3 "Continues in: EMR Connect › Manage › Reconnect a system"
goto g4 "Continues in: EMR Connect › Connect a system › Choose the system and contact"
goto g5 "Continues in: Settings › Agents › Change an agent's freedom"
goto g6 "Continues in: Settings › Pause › Pause one agent, resume all"

s1 --> q1
q1 -->|Reader| a1
q1 -->|Navigator| a2
a1 --> q2
a2 --> q2
q2 -->|Yes| t1 --> x1
q2 -->|No| q3
q3 -->|Ask before acting| o1 --> o2
o2 --> c1 --> x2
o2 --> c2 --> p1
q3 -->|Act, then report| p1
q3 -->|Act on its own| p1
p1 --> r1 --> q4
q4 -->|Yes| n1
q4 -->|No| t2
p1 -.-> g1 & g2 & g3 & g4
t1 -.-> g6
o2 -.-> g5
